@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="feed__head">
    <h1 class="feed__title">Privacy</h1>
</div>

<div class="prose">
    <p>
        Heardit stores your account (username, email address, a hash of your password if you set one, and
        your profile photo if you upload one) and everything you post: your ratings, your written reviews,
        the reviews you like, who you follow, your bio, your favorite tracks, and your listen-later queue.
        Reviews, follows, your bio, your photo and your favorites are visible to anyone else with an
        account. Your email address never is. A review shows how many likes it has, but not who liked it,
        and your queue is only shown to you. Nothing is sold or shared with anyone.
    </p>
    <p>
        Track players are embedded from spotify.com. Loading a page with a player means your browser talks
        to Spotify directly, and Spotify sets its own cookies and sees your IP address under
        <a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">its own privacy policy</a>.
        Heardit itself runs no analytics, no ad scripts, and no third-party trackers.
    </p>
    <p>
        Photos are cropped, shrunk and re-saved when you upload them, which strips everything else in the
        file, including the location a phone records. If you sign in with Google, Heardit receives your
        name, email address and whether Google has verified it, and keeps only the email and a Google
        account id to recognise you next time.
    </p>
    <p>
        Email is only ever sent to confirm your address, to reset your password, or to confirm a new
        address, and it goes out through Amazon's email service. You can delete your account, and
        everything attached to it, yourself from Settings. It's gone immediately.
    </p>
</div>
